Lab 3: Configuring Camel Routes with XML DSL
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Define and configure Apache Camel routes using XML Domain Specific Language (DSL)
Implement content-based routing and message transformation using XML DSL elements
Run a Camel context standalone (outside a container) and observe file-based route processing
Validate that routes are active and correctly processing messages using concrete file-count checks
Debug common XML DSL route configuration errors
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Apache Camel concepts (routes, endpoints, processors)
Familiarity with XML syntax and namespaces
Basic knowledge of enterprise integration patterns (content-based router, message translator)
Basic understanding of Java and Maven
